President Donald Trump said on Wednesday the United States may hit Iran's Pickaxe Mountain, warning them "not to get cute." He also commented that oil prices that have surged because of the Iran war likely won’t come down until after US midterm elections, as his advisors warned the conflict could extend through the remainder of his presidency. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0e64f78-acbf-11f1-9e76-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/42cbb3e1e32778b297d55ea54f6509aa2616b82e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0e64f78-acbf-11f1-9e76-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/42cbb3e1e32778b297d55ea54f6509aa2616b82e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e262c2c8-acc1-11f1-b41a-1d129a64eaee</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:46:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0e64f78-acbf-11f1-9e76-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/42cbb3e1e32778b297d55ea54f6509aa2616b82e.jpg">© Eric Lee, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>At least five killed, 87 missing after ferry fire in Philippines</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-at-least-five-killed-87-missing-after-ferry-fire-in-philippines</link><description>
At least five people died and 87 remained unaccounted for Thursday after a ferry caught fire off the Philippine island province of Palawan, with 42 passengers and crew rescued. Coast guard teams continued search and rescue operations as officials warned the figures could change while they worked to establish what happened.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de697182-acb0-11f1-848c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UR9VL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de697182-acb0-11f1-848c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UR9VL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60942422-acb6-11f1-ab5e-9924198a0345</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:24:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de697182-acb0-11f1-848c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UR9VL.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil Supreme Court chief suspends rival rulings amid election row</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-brazil-supreme-court-chief-suspends-rival-rulings-amid-election-row</link><description>
Brazil's Supreme Court chief justice stepped in Wednesday to halt conflicting rulings by two fellow judges as a dispute over alleged links between Justice Alexandre de Moraes and a fraud-accused banker deepened. The clash has spilled into the campaign for next month's presidential election, adding to tensions around the court.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78dd3878-aca4-11f1-aedf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247600235559.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78dd3878-aca4-11f1-aedf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247600235559.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73f60c82-aca8-11f1-b0c4-016c531905e6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 23:44:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78dd3878-aca4-11f1-aedf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247600235559.jpg">© Eraldo Peres, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Champions League: Iraola celebrates Liverpool win against Atletico Madrid</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260909-champions-league-iraola-celebrates-liverpool-win-against-atletico-madrid</link><description>
Liverpool began their Champions League campaign with a 2-1 comeback win over Atletico Madrid on Wednesday, giving new manager Andoni Iraola a winning start in Europe's top competition. Paris Saint-Germain, Barcelona and Arsenal also opened their campaigns with victories as the tournament's leading clubs got off the mark.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/703701e6-ac9e-11f1-a21b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/34a3f70569ebc08591ae0b4eef2163c1d378e2c5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/703701e6-ac9e-11f1-a21b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/34a3f70569ebc08591ae0b4eef2163c1d378e2c5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d336e2c-aca5-11f1-a077-ed93256507d2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 23:24:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/703701e6-ac9e-11f1-a21b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/34a3f70569ebc08591ae0b4eef2163c1d378e2c5.jpg">© Paul Ellis, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio to seek $45 million in additional security funding for Ecuador</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-to-seek-45-million-in-additional-security-funding-for-ecuador</link><description>
US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Wednesday that Washington would seek $45 million in additional security funding for Ecuador and provide military equipment as the two countries deepen cooperation against drug trafficking. During a visit to Quito, Rubio also announced new sanctions and a terrorist designation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32fa7e82-ac7d-11f1-9a34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a5421e17ec119b14a3a7062ebc329cd991951715.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32fa7e82-ac7d-11f1-9a34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a5421e17ec119b14a3a7062ebc329cd991951715.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7348bf2-aca1-11f1-8eca-ed93256507d2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 22:58:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32fa7e82-ac7d-11f1-9a34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a5421e17ec119b14a3a7062ebc329cd991951715.jpg">© Dolores Ochoa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Trump 'believes in the power of his own charisma', analyst says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260909-trump-believes-in-the-power-of-his-own-charisma-analyst-says</link><description>
Republicans opened their highly unusual midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday afternoon, a “Trump-a-Palooza” that is putting the president at the center of this fall’s midterm elections — whether the candidates running like it or not. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Professor Todd Belt, Director of the Political Management Programme at George Washington University, says that Trump "believes in the power of his own charisma".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02553b96-ac91-11f1-a87b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-223120-224354-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02553b96-ac91-11f1-a87b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-223120-224354-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce5dcefa-ac92-11f1-926b-4f97f44a989b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 21:09:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump claims firefighters carried him to safety ‘right after’ 9/11, but his account is disputed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-claims-firefighters-carried-him-to-safety-right-after-9-11-but-his-account-is-disputed-1</link><description>
As the 25th anniversary of 9/11 approaches, Donald Trump has lashed out at the press over coverage questioning where he was. This week, he said two firefighters carried him to safety near the US Steel Building right after the attacks, though he later said that he wasn’t at the World Trade Center on the day of the collapse. His version of events, and alleged role at Ground Zero have evolved many times over the years, as Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c458f60e-ac8e-11f1-a3bb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8387411906aa1c45bec0901-48181484.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c458f60e-ac8e-11f1-a3bb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8387411906aa1c45bec0901-48181484.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0bba7f0-ac8e-11f1-8fe7-fb408532d069</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 20:52:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Aid cuts force clinic closures across Sudan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/aid-cuts-force-clinic-closures-across-sudan</link><description>
In tonight's edition, funding cuts are forcing dozens of health clinics in Sudan to close, aid groups warn. Also, an AI and Africa conference has kicked off in South Korea's capital. And we have a poke around the Rwanda Space Agency as Paris hosts its very first international space summit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d2057a-ac8c-11f1-9189-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DN196627-A-01-20260901-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d2057a-ac8c-11f1-9189-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DN196627-A-01-20260901-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5b07b4d4-ac8d-11f1-95e9-7d148138b2ed</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 20:32:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran and US strike tankers in biggest shipping attack since war began</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260909-iran-and-us-strike-tankers-in-biggest-shipping-attack-since-war-began</link><description>
Iran and the US on Wednesday traded their biggest wave of attacks on shipping since the war began, with Iran saying it struck 10 vessels near the Strait of Hormuz after US forces sank five Iranian oil tankers. Brent crude oil surged above $100 a barrel as fears grew over global energy supplies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b63265d6-ac8b-11f1-81eb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T025208Z-1283160783-RC2EFNAYW0R4-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-CENTCOM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b63265d6-ac8b-11f1-81eb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T025208Z-1283160783-RC2EFNAYW0R4-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-CENTCOM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eeed3b22-ac8a-11f1-acc5-7d148138b2ed</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 20:31:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b63265d6-ac8b-11f1-81eb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T025208Z-1283160783-RC2EFNAYW0R4-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-CENTCOM.jpg">© US Central Command via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Passengers or pilots?' Europe looks to challenge US dominance in space sector with €10 billion plan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-passengers-or-pilots-europe-looks-to-challenge-us-dominance-in-space-sector-with-%E2%82%AC10-billion-plan</link><description>
Key figures from Europe’s space industry and other international players have converged on Paris to discuss how to advance the continent’s ambitions in a global market dominated by the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bcefa30-ac84-11f1-bc12-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T162013Z-1706368673-RC2SFNA0Y0TA-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-SPACE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bcefa30-ac84-11f1-bc12-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T162013Z-1706368673-RC2SFNA0Y0TA-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-SPACE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73cb5f16-ac79-11f1-b44b-5b3a02885cc3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 19:56:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bcefa30-ac84-11f1-bc12-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T162013Z-1706368673-RC2SFNA0Y0TA-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-SPACE.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthi offensive on Bab al-Mandeb may bring 'tremendous leverage', analyst explains</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-offensive-on-bab-al-mandeb-may-bring-tremendous-leverage-analyst-explains</link><description>
The Saudi-led coalition in Yemen on Wednesday said the Iran-backed Houthis had launched fresh attacks on the kingdom's south, after the rebels launched an offensive seeking to control the Bab al-Mandab Strait. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Adam Baron, Fellow at the New America Foundation, says that "if you have both groups able to disrupt maritime shipping both in the Red Sea and the Gulf, this would be a tremendous exercise of leverage to put pressure for a resolution".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45797214-8074-11f1-ae80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15T145635Z-188060635-RC2EEMAOW6BY-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-RED-SEA-SATELLITE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45797214-8074-11f1-ae80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15T145635Z-188060635-RC2EEMAOW6BY-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-RED-SEA-SATELLITE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">53c15c60-ac84-11f1-8363-61fe8a3e5a7f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 19:35:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU gives Spain 115 mn euros aid over Ceuta crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis</link><description>
The EU on Wednesday said it was granting Spain 115 million euros ($130 million) in emergency aid to help bolster border security and assist returns after the massive migrant rush into the north African exclave. More than 70,000 migrants crossed into Spanish territory from Morocco on July 30 and 31 in an unprecedented rush that left scores dead, most by drowning as they tried to swim around a breakwater. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62f5d27e-aa22-11f1-a7c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-ESPANA-CEUTA-CAMPAMENTO-MIGRANTES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62f5d27e-aa22-11f1-a7c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-ESPANA-CEUTA-CAMPAMENTO-MIGRANTES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">30224d0e-ac80-11f1-a2c6-f77bcad93d74</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 19:06:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Republicans put Trump center stage in US midterms gamble</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/republicans-put-trump-center-stage-in-us-midterms-gamble</link><description>
US Republicans open an extraordinary midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday betting that putting Donald Trump at the center of their campaign can rescue a party facing grim election forecasts -- despite the president's deeply negative approval ratings. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e568c03a-ac67-11f1-94b2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T030521Z-656306742-RC2OYK97ENYA-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-REPUBLICANS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e568c03a-ac67-11f1-94b2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T030521Z-656306742-RC2OYK97ENYA-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-REPUBLICANS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c6b8226-ac80-11f1-b60f-f77bcad93d74</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 19:04:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Whose space is it? Europe scrambles as US rules satellite race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260909-whose-space-is-it-europe-scrambles-as-us-rules-satellite-race</link><description>
With the digital age comes the scramble for minerals below us and the scramble to master the heavens above us. Donald Trump wants a thousand rocket launches a year and with SpaceX’s reusable modules leading the way, the United States towers over the competition. It’s why for instance Ukraine’s president has to beg Elon Musk to use his Starlink low orbit satellite system to take out the Russian cruise missile launchers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94c5ddc4-ac77-11f1-a256-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T162116Z-134763298-RC2RFNARCBVB-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-SPACE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94c5ddc4-ac77-11f1-a256-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T162116Z-134763298-RC2RFNARCBVB-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-SPACE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97d1ee4e-ac78-11f1-a0f6-e5b53430e772</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 18:35:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran strikes ships, expands no-go zone outside Hormuz strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait</link><description>
Iran said it attacked more than a dozen vessels trying to pass through the Strait of Hormuz on Wednesday, as it announced an expansion of a no-go zone outside the strategic waterway it has blockaded for months. The fresh attacks and fighting with the United States have sent oil prices above $100 per barrel again as Tehran chokes off the strait and Washington presses a counter-blockade of Iranian ports. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c7acabb0-ac7b-11f1-94e1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-200236-200652-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c7acabb0-ac7b-11f1-94e1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-200236-200652-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cd199766-ac7b-11f1-937b-5b3a02885cc3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 18:30:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>How a French Foreign Legion soldier dramatically escaped Colombian captors</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-how-a-french-foreign-legion-soldier-dramatically-escaped-colombian-captors</link><description>
A French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped by Colombian guerrillas escaped after nearly a month in captivity by overpowering a guard, jumping into a river with his hands tied and trekking for four days through the Andes to reach safety, according to a Colombian military source.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cbe6028-ac66-11f1-94f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7LM6NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cbe6028-ac66-11f1-94f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7LM6NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24c2d00e-ac68-11f1-86c7-8d898541b3b4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 16:17:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cbe6028-ac66-11f1-94f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7LM6NQ.jpg">© Handout via Colombian Military Forces, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya's crackdown on foreign workers raises concern among Burundians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-kenya-s-crackdown-on-foreign-workers-raises-concern-among-burundians</link><description>
Some 16,000 Burundian refugees and asylum seekers live in Kenya, and many of them make a living through informal jobs – as carpenters, motorcycle taxi drivers, or clothing vendors. But since Monday, many have been afraid to go to work, and are now looking to leave the country. The reason: remarks made by Kenya’s president, which have sparked deep concern within the Burundian community. More from our correspondent Bastien Renouil.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/634c26da-ac64-11f1-a773-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-214432-214606-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/634c26da-ac64-11f1-a773-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-214432-214606-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">691a9c2c-ac64-11f1-97a7-abc6370ac198</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:47:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Céline Dion's return to France: A French love affair</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-c%C3%A9line-dion-s-return-to-france-a-french-love-affair</link><description>
Céline Dion’s hotly anticipated return to the stage is scheduled for this Saturday in Paris – the first of more than 16 concerts in the French capital in September and October. The shows mark a major milestone for 58-year-old Dion after years away from touring due to a rare neurological disorder. FRANCE 24's Aurore Cloé Dupuis tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8db3b614-ac63-11f1-b5dc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-162112-162742-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8db3b614-ac63-11f1-b5dc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-162112-162742-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93344cca-ac63-11f1-8031-5d0802230573</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:33:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron summit seeks boost for European space despite no-shows</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-macron-summit-seeks-boost-for-european-space-despite-no-shows</link><description>
France is pressing ahead with a space summit shunned by the US tech giants and hampered by a lower-than-expected turnout from European leaders as President Emmanuel Macron seeks a stronger role for Europe in the competitive maelstrom of space. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3be5bbf8-ac62-11f1-8e71-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-161638-162111-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3be5bbf8-ac62-11f1-8e71-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-161638-162111-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">40ad4cf0-ac62-11f1-a946-abc6370ac198</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:32:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>NY failed to disclose what it knew on 'toxic air' after 9/11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-ny-failed-to-disclose-what-it-knew-on-toxic-air-after-9-11</link><description>
New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani announced on Tuesday the release of tens of thousands of documents showing the city did not disclose all it knew about air toxicity after 9/11. The release comes ahead of the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001, attacks that killed 2,977 people in the United States, mostly in the collapse of the Twin Towers in New York. In the years since, more than 9,400 have died from illnesses linked to their exposure to the area, according to a federal medical monitoring program.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2052c7d2-ac62-11f1-92d9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-160146-160348-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2052c7d2-ac62-11f1-92d9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-160146-160348-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2521d8f2-ac62-11f1-b9d6-5d0802230573</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:30:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Peru: 38 skeletons unearthed in ancient tomb</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-peru-38-skeletons-unearthed-in-ancient-tomb</link><description>
Archaeologists in Peru have discovered a near-intact pre-Incan tomb, containing the skeletons of 38 individuals, along with gold and copper objects. The remains include those of an elite member of the Chimu civilization, which flourished between 900 and 1470 AD.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33674d0e-ac60-11f1-948e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Peru-tomb-thumbnail.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33674d0e-ac60-11f1-948e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Peru-tomb-thumbnail.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17f409ae-ac60-11f1-9080-5d0802230573</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:21:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's far-right National Rally fires policeman from security team over racist, sexist comments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-france-s-far-right-national-rally-fires-policeman-from-security-team-over-racist-sexist-comments</link><description>
France's far-right National Rally (RN) has expelled a policeman from its ranks after bodycam footage of him making racist, homophobic and sexist remarks was published on Wednesday. The controversy threatens to revive scrutiny of the party's efforts to distance itself from its extremist past ahead of next year's presidential election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfc781e0-ac5d-11f1-b96b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96J76G4-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfc781e0-ac5d-11f1-b96b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96J76G4-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a4e1b38a-ac5f-11f1-87f6-5d0802230573</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:16:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfc781e0-ac5d-11f1-b96b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-96J76G4-1.jpg">© Valentine Chapuis, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>‘Call My Agent’ returns: George Clooney, Eva Longoria guest star in French film spinoff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260909-call-my-agent-returns-george-clooney-eva-longoria-guest-star-in-french-film-spinoff</link><description>
Manon Kerjean, FRANCE 24's film critic highlights some of her picks among the French films in competition at the 83rd Venice International Film Festival. She also looks at new releases in French cinema: "15/18", a film set in a psychiatric unit which tackles mental health and "A Woman's Life" – a film starring Cesar-winning actress Léa Drucker as a woman whose organized life is upended by the arrival of a stranger. She also previews "The Unknown", a film by Arthur Hariri about two strangers who wake up in each other's bodies. Finally, she gives her thoughts on a highly anticipated film, "Call my Agent", which picks up five years after the end of the hit TV series on Netflix. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd57b4ea-ac59-11f1-a5c9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12099828776aa16b9a89e8e3-95273250.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd57b4ea-ac59-11f1-a5c9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12099828776aa16b9a89e8e3-95273250.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e9a18e2-ac59-11f1-96db-f701434f55f3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 14:29:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
